# Cloudflare Workers + Static Assets routing for dynamic SPA routes.
#
# Background: `not_found_handling: "single-page-application"` in
# wrangler.jsonc serves the root /index.html on any 404 — wrong for
# /trasy/<slug>/ and /szczyty/<slug>/, which need their per-route shell so
# useParams() can read the slug and TripDetailRoute / PeakDetailRoute can
# resolve the manifest.
#
# Cloudflare Workers Assets validates _redirects at deploy time and
# rejects destinations that would normalise back into the source pattern
# (error 10021 "infinite loop"). So pointing at /trasy/_/index.html does
# NOT work — Cloudflare strips /index.html, sees /trasy/_/ which matches
# /trasy/* again, refuses the deploy.
#
# Fix: postbuild script `apps/web/scripts/copy-spa-shells.mjs` copies the
# Next-emitted placeholder shells to /_shells/trasy.html and
# /_shells/szczyty.html. Those paths sit outside any redirect source so
# the validator is happy. The HTML is identical — JS bundles are loaded
# by absolute /_next/* paths, so it doesn't matter which directory served
# the file. useParams() reads from window.location, which Cloudflare
# leaves untouched on a 200 rewrite.

/trasy/*    /_shells/trasy.html    200
/szczyty/*  /_shells/szczyty.html  200
